<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</span><h2>Through our five-step process</h2><p>Every identity project follows the same five-step process — Discover, Plan, Build, Launch, Grow — so the design is grounded in strategy before a single mark is drawn.</p></div>
<div class="values">
<article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Discover</h3><p>We learn about your business, your customers and your competitors, and agree what the brand needs to say.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Plan</h3><p>Positioning, naming direction and a clear scope: what will be designed, in what order, and for which materials.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Logo, colour, typography and applications, developed in rounds with your feedback at each stage.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Launch</h3><p>Guidelines and final files delivered, ready for your <a href="/expertise-web-development/">website</a>, your social channels and your print materials.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>05</span><h3>Grow</h3><p>As your business adds products or enters new markets, the identity flexes — and we stay on hand to extend it.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">QUESTIONS</span><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
<div class="values">
<article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>What does a brand identity include?</h3><p>A logo, colour palette, typography and visual language, plus guidelines that show how to use them. Depending on your needs, it can also cover stationery, brochures, presentation templates, packaging and signage.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Can you redesign an existing logo?</h3><p>Yes. Many of our identity projects start with a logo or brand that no longer fits the business. We keep what still works, update what doesn’t, and make sure the change is clear to your customers.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Do you design for print as well as digital?</h3><p>Yes. We design brochures, exhibition graphics, packaging and signage alongside digital assets, so your identity stays consistent wherever people meet your business.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>How long does a brand identity project take?</h3><p>It depends on scope — a logo alone is quicker than a full identity with guidelines and printed materials. We agree deliverables and a timeline after our first conversation, before work begins.</p></article>
